use "@std"
use "@audio"

Note: ===== SPIKE C3: EnvelopeProcessor div-by-zero on sub-frame durations =====
Note: Reference: flow-lang/StandardLibrary/Audio/EnvelopeProcessor.cs lines 108, 120, 150, 156, 169
Note: Audit hypothesis (C3): `(float)i / attackFrames` divides by zero when any envelope
Note: segment duration rounds to 0 frames (very short attacks/releases or very low sample rates).
Note: Architecture hypothesis: `for (int i = 0; i < attackFrames; i++)` never runs when
Note: attackFrames == 0, so the division inside the body is unreachable.

Note: Reachability confirmed by grep:
Note:   flow-lang/StandardLibrary/BuiltInFunctions.cs:532 registers createAR
Note:   flow-lang/StandardLibrary/BuiltInFunctions.cs:537 registers createADSR
Note:   flow-lang/StandardLibrary/BuiltInFunctions.cs:542 registers applyEnvelope
Note: So user .flow code CAN drive these code paths with arbitrary sample rates.

Note: ===== Probe construction notes =====
Note: Buffer: 4410 frames of stereo silence at SR=44100 (0.1 sec).
Note: Attack 0.00001 sec * 44100 = 0.441 -> (int) truncates to 0 attackFrames.
Note: Decay / release same math.
Note: If C3 is real (pitfalls agent hypothesis), the probes below will raise a
Note: DivideByZeroException or write NaN into the output buffer.
Note: If C3 is false positive (architecture agent hypothesis), every probe prints its
Note: survived sentinel and the program exits cleanly with code 0.

Int SR = 44100
Int CHANNELS = 2
Int FRAMES = 4410

Note: --- Probe 1: AR envelope with sub-frame attack, normal release ---
Note: Targets line 108: curve[frame] = (float)i / attackFrames with attackFrames == 0.
Buffer b1 = (createBuffer FRAMES CHANNELS SR)
Double zero = (intToDouble 0)
Double one = (intToDouble 1)
(fillBuffer b1 one)
Envelope e1 = (createAR 0.00001 0.05 SR)
(applyEnvelope b1 e1)
(print "c3-probe1-survived")

Note: --- Probe 2: AR envelope with BOTH sub-frame attack AND sub-frame release ---
Note: Targets both line 108 AND line 120 in one pass.
Buffer b2 = (createBuffer FRAMES CHANNELS SR)
(fillBuffer b2 one)
Envelope e2 = (createAR 0.00001 0.00001 SR)
(applyEnvelope b2 e2)
(print "c3-probe2-survived")

Note: --- Probe 3: ADSR with every segment sub-frame ---
Note: Targets lines 150, 156, and 169 simultaneously.
Buffer b3 = (createBuffer FRAMES CHANNELS SR)
(fillBuffer b3 one)
Envelope e3 = (createADSR 0.00001 0.00001 0.8 0.00001 SR)
(applyEnvelope b3 e3)
(print "c3-probe3-survived")

Note: --- Probe 4: low sample rate so that even a 1ms attack truncates to 0 frames ---
Note: SR=100, 0.001 sec * 100 = 0.1 frames -> truncates to 0.
Int LOW_SR = 100
Int LOW_FRAMES = 200
Buffer b4 = (createBuffer LOW_FRAMES CHANNELS LOW_SR)
(fillBuffer b4 one)
Envelope e4 = (createAR 0.001 0.001 LOW_SR)
(applyEnvelope b4 e4)
(print "c3-probe4-survived")

Note: --- Probe 5: ADSR at low sample rate, all segments sub-frame ---
Buffer b5 = (createBuffer LOW_FRAMES CHANNELS LOW_SR)
(fillBuffer b5 one)
Envelope e5 = (createADSR 0.001 0.001 0.5 0.001 LOW_SR)
(applyEnvelope b5 e5)
(print "c3-probe5-survived")

Note: --- Probe 6: control -- normal durations MUST also work (regression guard) ---
Buffer b6 = (createBuffer FRAMES CHANNELS SR)
(fillBuffer b6 one)
Envelope e6 = (createAR 0.01 0.02 SR)
(applyEnvelope b6 e6)
(print "c3-probe6-survived")

(print "c3-all-probes-complete")

Note: ===== Expected output under hypothesis "C3 is Dismissed" (architecture agent) =====
Note:   c3-probe1-survived
Note:   c3-probe2-survived
Note:   c3-probe3-survived
Note:   c3-probe4-survived
Note:   c3-probe5-survived
Note:   c3-probe6-survived
Note:   c3-all-probes-complete
Note:
Note: ===== Expected output under hypothesis "C3 is Confirmed" (pitfalls agent) =====
Note:   Any missing "probeN-survived" line plus a DivideByZeroException on stderr.
Note:   A renderer crash on any of probes 1-5 would confirm the audit claim.
